WIRESHARK NETWORK PROTOCOL ANALYSIS

Project Domain: Computer Networks & Cybersecurity
Tool: Wireshark
Project Type: Network Traffic Analysis
Level: Beginner to Intermediate

ABSTRACT

Network communication plays an essential role in modern computing. Different protocols work together to enable communication between devices over local and global networks.

This project focuses on analyzing network traffic using Wireshark, an open-source packet analysis tool. It examines commonly used network protocols, including TCP, UDP, DNS, HTTP, HTTPS, ARP, DHCP, ICMP, and TLS.

The project demonstrates packet capturing, protocol identification, display filtering, and network traffic inspection. It also discusses common network security observations and the importance of encrypted communication.

1. INTRODUCTION

Wireshark is a widely used network protocol analyzer that allows users to capture and inspect packets transmitted across a network.

It provides detailed information about network communication, including source and destination addresses, ports, protocols, packet lengths, and protocol-specific fields.

Wireshark is useful for:

Network troubleshooting.
Protocol analysis.
Cybersecurity investigations.
Network performance monitoring.
Educational networking experiments.
